Please find MC response below:

The report shows that SGBL is non-compliant for money send transactions.
 
This is related on what SGBL sends in DE42.
Mastercard considers transactions noncompliant when any of these subedits apply:
 
 
 
a. Data Element (DE) 122 (Additional Data), subelement 001 (Additional Acceptor Data), subfield 003 (Acceptor URL address) is not populated and DE 22 (Point-of-Service [POS] Entry Mode), subfield 1 (POS Terminal PAN Entry Mode) is one of these:
 
 
 
09 (PAN/Token entry through electronic commerce containing DSRP cryptogram in DE 55 (Integrated Circuit Card [ICC] System-Related Data)
 
10 (Credential on File)
 
81 (PAN/Token entry through electronic commerce with optional Identity Check-AAV in DE 48, subelement 43 [UCAF] or DSRP cryptogram in DE 104, subelement 001 [Digital Payment Cryptogram])
 
82 (Electronic Commerce PAN Auto Entry through Server [issuer, acquirer, or third-party vendor System])
 
b. DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 003 is populated and does not contain a period or does not contain at least one alphanumeric character before the period and at least two alpha characters after the period or contains a space or @ character.
 
c. DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 004 (Acceptor Customer Service Phone Number) is not populated and all of these are true:
 
DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 003 is not populated
 
DE 22, subfield 1 is not equal to 09, 10, 81, or 82
 
d. DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 004 is populated and
 
DE 43 (Acceptor Name and Location), subfield 5 (Acceptor Country Code) is USA or CAN and DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 004 is not 10 positions with the first three positions being numeric or
 
DE 122, subelement 001, subfield 004 is not between five and fifteen numeric characters (excluding Canada and the United States).
 
Exclusions:
 
Mastercard defined airline travel transactions; DE 18 (Acceptor Business Code [MCC]) equal to 4511 or is within the range 3000 to 3350
 
DE 48 (Additional Data: Private Use), subelement 77 (Transaction Type Identifier) is:
 
C67 (Mastercard Merchant Presented QR)
 
C68 (Mastercard Merchant Presented QR Refund)
 
DE 61 (Point-of-Service [POS] Data), subfield 7 (POS Transaction Status) is 8 (Account Status Inquiry Service [ASI])
 
DE 121 (Authorizing Agent ID Code) is 000000 (MIP X-Code System)
 
 Sharing a sample,
DE122S01F03 Acpt URL addr https://win2.ro
 
So similar URL is missing from the sample,
 
For the authorization or financial request, SEND must map the API value to:
DE122 / SE001 / SF003 = Acceptor URL Address
The implementation requirement explicitly states that Acceptor URL is mandatory for CNP/e-commerce transactions and that the value is propagated into DE122.001.003.
 You will need to refer to your operation development team to work on this.
